From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Morris <jmorris@namei.org>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] lib: sbi: add the experimental domain commit extension

Add an experimental SBI extension, 0x08004246, with two functions.

Function 0 commits the calling hart to its run-time domain. The hart
must run in the non-root domain of least initialization order that
lists it, exactly one other non-root domain must list it, and that
domain must name the hart as its boot hart and have an SBI call
allowlist. The function reads no argument: the target follows from the
domains of the device tree and the hart that calls. The decision is a
pure function of the domains as the hart sees them. If it holds, the
hart leaves its domain through sbi_domain_context_exit(), which enters
the target at its next address in its next mode; otherwise the call
returns SBI_ERR_DENIED and changes nothing. Since the target has the
greater initialization order, no hart can commit back.

Function 1 returns one word of the configuration digest read from the
device tree, most significant word first. It is served only to a hart
in a non-root domain without an allowlist, the domain a hart boots in.

Whenever the memory protection of a hart is configured for a domain
with an allowlist, at a switch, a warm boot or a resume, the hart's
menvcfg.CBIE is cleared, so that cache-block invalidation is illegal
below M-mode, and the PMP entries are checked against the domain's
regions. A mismatch fails the configuration, which stops the hart. The
commit record then keeps menvcfg, mseccfg and the first PMP entries.

AI-assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), in the GitHub Copilot CLI
